Dear Soren,

An update on the kitchen cabinets at 42 Brackenveil Row, Oakhollow. You asked us to obtain a quote for replacing the laminate.

The joiner, Alderline Joinery, told us by phone today that the laminate is peeling from several panels. In their view, replacing it properly would mean stripping the kitchen, so they think a new kitchen is the practical option. They have given no figures and no written estimate yet. They also say earlier prices may have changed.

I have asked them for a written quote with two separate prices, laminate and door repair only, and a new kitchen, each stating what is included and whether VAT is included. I will send you both as soon as I have them. Nothing has been approved or started, and no cost is committed. Our earlier requests for your approval of an inspection visit are still open, so please reply if you would like to approve it.

The tenant has reported cuts from the sharp laminate edges, so a prompt decision will help.

Kind regards,
Nia Calder
